  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Homeowners insurance in Utah covers a roof leak only if it results from a sudden, accidental event caused by a covered peril."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\u2705 What Is Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Storm Damage: Leaks caused by severe wind, hail, or heavy snow/ice weight."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Falling Objects: Damage from fallen trees, large tree limbs, or debris."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fire or Lightning: Direct fire or lightning impact that breaches the roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Interior Water Damage: Resulting ruin to drywall, ceilings, or personal property, minus your deductible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\u26a0\ufe0f What Is Not Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wear and Tear: Leaks due to an old or aging roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Lack of Maintenance: Ignored missing shingles, cracked flashing, or rotted wood."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Gradual Seepage: Slow leaks that have dripped over weeks or months."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Earthquakes or Floods: Standard policies exclude earth movement and surface flooding (requires separate policies)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udccc What to Do Next"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Document Everything: Take clear photos and videos of the exterior roof damage and interior water leaks."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Prevent More Damage: Place buckets and tarps to stop further water spread (insurers expect mitigation)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review Your Deductible: Compare repair costs against your policy deductible before filing. If you have questions or disputes, you can reach out to the Utah Insurance Department at 800-439-3805.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
                "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What caused the leak (a recent storm, aging shingles, etc.)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The age of your roof?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you figure out if filing a claim makes financial sense for your situation."
      }
    ],
